{
 "manufacturer": "Vaisala",
 "manufacturer_slug": "vaisala",
 "model": "Indigo510 / Indigo520 transmitters (Modbus TCP)",
 "model_slug": "indigo510-indigo520",
 "short_model": "Indigo520",
 "aliases": [
  "Indigo510",
  "Indigo520",
  "Indigo500 series"
 ],
 "equipment_type": "Sensor transmitter (host for Vaisala probes)",
 "applies_to": "Indigo510 and Indigo520 transmitter registers (unit ID 240) over Modbus TCP (user guide M212287EN-AJ).",
 "summary": "Indigo510 and Indigo520 are Vaisala transmitters that host one or two smart probes (humidity, CO2, dew point, H2O2 and others) and expose them over Modbus TCP, analog outputs and relays. This map covers the transmitter itself at unit ID 240: optional barometer and analog input, analog output and relay configuration, network and clock settings.",
 "transport": [
  "TCP"
 ],
 "defaults": {
  "unit_id": 240,
  "baud": null,
  "parity": null,
  "data_bits": null,
  "stop_bits": null,
  "tcp_port": 502
 },
 "addressing": {
  "convention": "1-based",
  "note": "The guide numbers registers in decimal starting at 1 and also prints the 0-based hex address used in the request; register number 1 is address 0x0000 on the wire."
 },
 "default_word_order": "CDAB",
 "firmware": null,
 "source": {
  "title": "Indigo510, Indigo520 User Guide",
  "doc_number": "M212287EN-AJ",
  "revision_date": "2026-10",
  "url": "https://docs.vaisala.com/r/M212287EN-AJ/en-US",
  "pages": "Chapter 10 Modbus pp. 177-178; Appendix A Modbus reference pp. 203-219 (Tables 37-48)"
 },
 "notes": [
  "Transmitter registers are holding registers on unit ID 240: read with function 03, write with function 16.",
  "32-bit floats put the least significant word at the listed register (CDAB). The guide states this, and its worked example (30.56 %RH read from a probe at unit ID 241) confirms it.",
  "Unavailable data reads as quiet NaN (float) or 0x8000 (16-bit integer) rather than an exception.",
  "Probe readings are not in this map: read the probe on unit ID 241 (terminal 1) or 242 (terminal 2) using that probe's own register map.",
  "Modbus TCP read and write access are both disabled by default and must be enabled on the touchscreen or web interface.",
  "Indigo510 has 2 analog outputs; Indigo520 has 4 analog outputs, an analog input and 2 relays (the analog input, outputs and relays are not available on PoE-powered Indigo520 units). Registers for hardware a unit lacks are not useful on it.",
  "Left out: analog output clipping limits, NTP address and DNS server strings, the time-zone enum (91 values) and the test registers.",
  "Network strings occupy 8 registers for up to 15 characters."
 ],
